Jim Morrison alive.

483
00:21:59,639 --> 00:22:02,108
Yeah, I had no cell all day.
I got like 25 messages!

484
00:22:02,174 --> 00:22:03,949
- What's going on?
- Nothing that exciting.

485
00:22:04,043 --> 00:22:06,184
Just an emergency meeting
with the head of the studio

486
00:22:06,268 --> 00:22:07,949
on the Billy Walsh/Vinny Chase project.

487
00:22:08,043 --> 00:22:09,959
- What's the problem?
- Would you like to know?

488
00:22:10,043 --> 00:22:12,175
- Ari!
- You snooze, you lose. I gotta go!

489
00:22:18,004 --> 00:22:19,957
- What the hell is going on?
- Desperate times

490
00:22:20,023 --> 00:22:21,582
call for desperate measures here.

491
00:22:21,675 --> 00:22:22,774
Thank God I'm in a robe.

492
00:22:22,872 --> 00:22:25,069
And, may I comment on
what lovely ankles you have!

493
00:22:25,134 --> 00:22:27,397
- Talk fast, Ari.
- You don't have your summer movie?

494
00:22:27,794 --> 00:22:30,085
- Come again?
- At ten poll, you don't have one!

495
00:22:30,480 --> 00:22:31,522
I have <i>Clouds!</i>

496
00:22:31,649 --> 00:22:33,686
Billy Walsh and Vinny Chase
don't wanna do it.

497
00:22:33,972 --> 00:22:35,381
Where the hell is Dana Gordon?

498
00:22:35,456 --> 00:22:38,412
I'm right outside the door, Richard!
Ari locked me out!

499
00:22:38,699 --> 00:22:39,704
Let her in!

500
00:22:42,852 --> 00:22:44,486
- Hey, Dana!
- Fuck you, Ari!

501
00:22:44,561 --> 00:22:46,181
What's the hell's going on with <i>Clouds</i>?

502
00:22:46,265 --> 00:22:48,462
I'm working on it.
When you return from New York,

503
00:22:48,528 --> 00:22:50,209
I'll have
a completely new team in place.

504
00:22:50,298 --> 00:22:53,293
Impossible! Billy burned 6 weeks
writing the wrong script.

505
00:22:53,410 --> 00:22:56,509
And you don't have enough time to put
<i>Clouds</i> back on board

506
00:22:56,576 --> 00:22:57,606
for your July release.

507
00:22:57,672 --> 00:22:59,578
You and your friend Billy Walsh
are dear!

508
00:22:59,719 --> 00:23:01,860
No, we are not dead.
We are very much alive.

509
00:23:01,935 --> 00:23:05,202
You, with your fading star prizes
and your 3 straight quarters in the red

510
00:23:05,307 --> 00:23:07,445
are dead if you're to go
to your board of directors,

511
00:23:07,494 --> 00:23:10,062
and tell them that this summer
may be a worse quarter yet.

512
00:23:10,137 --> 00:23:11,480
I'm gonna tear your head off!

513
00:23:11,555 --> 00:23:13,884
Please don't,
because I have your summer movie.

514
00:23:14,790 --> 00:23:18,698
From the director of <i>Medellin</i>
and <i>Queens Boulevard,</i> comes <i>Silo</i>.

515
00:23:19,038 --> 00:23:22,595
It is the story of a group
of non unionized farmhands

516
00:23:22,736 --> 00:23:26,081
who band together
to survive a nuclear attack

517
00:23:26,163 --> 00:23:28,985
after discovering
an underground society.

518
00:23:29,135 --> 00:23:30,271
It's ready to shoot.

519
00:23:30,355 --> 00:23:32,862
Billy Walsh's on board,
Vinny Chase is on board,

520
00:23:32,921 --> 00:23:36,646
and if you're not,
Fox, Universal and Sony are.

521
00:23:36,893 --> 00:23:37,904
He's bluffing.

522
00:23:38,026 --> 00:23:40,076
What's it matter?
There's a summer movie in there,

523
00:23:40,156 --> 00:23:41,508
we pack up our shit and go home!

524
00:23:42,155 --> 00:23:45,015
Tell him how good it is, Dana.
All personal bullshit aside.

525
00:23:49,090 --> 00:23:51,466
- It's an excellent script.
- Can we market it!

526
00:23:53,288 --> 00:23:56,058
Think... <i>Blade Runner</i>
meets <i>Field of Dreams</i>.

527
00:23:56,133 --> 00:23:57,663
Two classics! Boom!

528
00:23:58,330 --> 00:23:59,602
You make this good, Dana.

529
00:23:59,973 --> 00:24:02,097
And you, Ari, this I don't soon forget.

530
00:24:04,962 --> 00:24:07,351
That was unbelievable.
<i>Blade Runner</i> meets <i>Field of Dreams</i>?

531
00:24:07,389 --> 00:24:09,560
- Not bad, huh?
- You actually read it?

532
00:24:09,620 --> 00:24:11,901
What do we need to read it for?
I'll go to the movies!

533
00:24:11,986 --> 00:24:13,021
We have a gold movie!

534
00:24:13,094 --> 00:24:15,028
Die, Ari! I truly hope you die!

535
00:24:16,788 --> 00:24:18,009
Did I do it, Vinny?

536
00:24:18,094 --> 00:24:19,741
Yes, you did, and thank you.

537
00:24:20,004 --> 00:24:22,361
So... Any possibility of shooting this

538
00:24:22,408 --> 00:24:24,685
a little closer to civilization,
Bill, please?

539
00:24:24,816 --> 00:24:27,120
It takes place on a farm
in Nova Scotia, Turtle.

540
00:24:27,286 --> 00:24:29,586
Ignore him, Billy.
He read every third page.

541
00:24:29,765 --> 00:24:31,389
I, on the other hand, was riveted!

542
00:24:31,906 --> 00:24:34,704
Especially by the character
of Kelton, the farmhand.

543
00:24:34,798 --> 00:24:36,704
Yeah, I was thinking of you
when I wrote that.

544
00:24:37,235 --> 00:24:38,597
- Really?
- No.

545
00:24:39,544 --> 00:24:40,624
How about a toast?

546
00:24:40,831 --> 00:24:44,032
To a groundbreaking day
and a possibly groundbreaking movie!

547
00:24:44,351 --> 00:24:46,473
Are you kissing my ass,
now, snake suit?

548
00:24:46,539 --> 00:24:49,254
Come on, Billy! He came through.
You can't stay mad at him!

549
00:24:49,339 --> 00:24:52,100
Well, I'm no longer planning on
using your car as a toilet,

550
00:24:52,156 --> 00:24:53,959
but I'll get back to you
by being my agent.

551
00:24:54,024 --> 00:24:56,259
I wait with bated breath, Sir!

552
00:24:57,601 --> 00:24:59,263
Why does nobody answer their cells?

553
00:24:59,348 --> 00:25:00,437
Look who's talking!

554
00:25:00,512 --> 00:25:01,742
Where have you been, E.?

555
00:25:01,817 --> 00:25:03,772
Too busy being professional
with your girlfriend

556
00:25:03,821 --> 00:25:06,155
- to pick up the phone?
- Please, tell me what's going on.

557
00:25:06,218 --> 00:25:08,314
Don't stress your pretty little head
about it!

558
00:25:08,480 --> 00:25:10,424
- It's all been handled.
- What's been handled?

559
00:25:10,508 --> 00:25:11,738
We're making Billy's movie.

560
00:25:14,198 --> 00:25:15,252
<i>Silo</i>?

561
00:25:17,617 --> 00:25:18,739
Where is the snow?

